      "narration": "Priya adds disability coverage for her twenty employees. A group plan differs from Rosa’s individual policy in predictable ways. The employer holds the master contract and often pays the premium. There is no individual medical underwriting; everyone in the class is covered. Benefits are a percentage of salary rather than a chosen dollar amount, with a monthly maximum. Coverage is usually nonoccupational and offsets Social Security and workers compensation. Definitions tend to be split: own occupation for two years, then any occupation. If the employer pays the premium, benefits are taxable. Coverage ends when employment ends, though some plans allow conversion.",
